  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsible Business Conduct (RBC) support center</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dutch companies are expected to exercise due diligence to identify, prevent or mitigate risks to people and the environment, and to be accountable for how they address wrongdoing. The RBC support center is designed to help companies avoid and address abuses related to their operations, value chains and other business relationships in this way. The international frameworks recommend a risk-based approach, meaning that companies should first address the most serious risks and impacts in their value chains. As such, an impact is particularly expected in OECD-DAC countries, where governance gaps exist because relevant laws may be missing and/or implementation deficient.Specifically, the support center will focus on:- General information on the OECD guidelines, upcoming legislation, and what is expected of companies in a general sense.- Specific information and advice on the specific needs of individual companies.- Practical advice, support and translation of what the above points mean in concrete terms for the company.- Coordination of knowledge about the available guidelines, tools, roadmaps, training, and relevant partners already present in the IMVO landscape - and possibly developing new ones where necessary.- Active referral to partners and stakeholders if a request for help requires special specialised knowledge or depth.</narrative>
  </description>
